#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183952 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86cc32d1-5444-5deb-9168-ba67cd8d0e69" :knowledge-point/title "Quadratic Functions Containing an Isolated Perfect Square"}] :question/id #uuid "af43cc58-820d-5f4c-9ab8-e3a8c05bcee0" :question/math-academy-id "e-14873" :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x) = (x+4)^2 -3$ for $x\\geq -4$?" :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny = (x+4)^2 -3\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx = (y+4)^2 -3\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= (y + 4)^{2} - 3 \\\\\nx + 3 &= (y + 4)^{2} \\\\\n\\sqrt{x + 3} &= y + 4 \\\\\n\\sqrt{x + 3} - 4 &= y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the positive square root because if\n\n$$\nx \\geq -4\n$$\n\nis the domain of $f$, then the range of the inverse is\n\n$$\nf^{-1} \\geq -4\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with $f^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{x + 3} - 4\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183953 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184165 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "50718b79-529c-5515-bfa2-dbb8b97f4a4a" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Inverse by Completing the Square"}] :question/id #uuid "28859a1c-7f0d-58f2-8c77-ff4e27cf610d" :question/math-academy-id "e-14877" :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x) = -x^2 + 2x + 6$ for $x\\geq 1$?" :question/worked-solution "First, we complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(x) &= -x^{2} + 2x + 6 \\\\\n&= - (x^{2} - 2x) + 6 \\\\\n&= - (x^{2} - 2 \\cdot x + 1^{2} - 1^{2}) + 6 \\\\\n&= - ((x - 1)^{2} - 1) + 6 \\\\\n&= - (x - 1)^{2} + 1 + 6 \\\\\n&= - (x - 1)^{2} + 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$.\n\n$$\ny = -(x-1)^2+ 7\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$.\n\n$$\nx = -(y-1)^2+ 7\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= - (y - 1)^{2} + 7 \\\\\nx - 7 &= - (y - 1)^{2} \\\\\n7 - x &= (y - 1)^{2} \\\\\n\\sqrt{7 - x} &= y - 1 \\\\\n\\sqrt{7 - x} + 1 &= y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we selected the positive square root because if the domain of $f(x)$ is\n\n$$\nx \\geq 1\n$$\n\nthen the range of $f^{-1}(x)$ is\n\n$$\nf^{-1} \\geq 1\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with $f^{-1}(x)$.\n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{7-x} +1\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186183954 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02655639-b390-510d-9eda-3221375e7e5e" :knowledge-point/title "The Negative Square Root Case"}] :question/id #uuid "836ac184-e55d-5c32-a4af-8a0da847a423" :question/math-academy-id "e-14879" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x) = (x - 3)^2 - 2$ for $x \\leq 3$." :question/worked-solution "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y{:}$\n\n$$\ny = (x-3)^2 - 2\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y{:}$\n\n$$\nx = (y - 3)^2 - 2\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &= (y - 3)^{2} - 2 \\\\\nx + 2 &= (y - 3)^{2} \\\\\n- \\sqrt{x + 2} &= y - 3 \\\\\n3 - \\sqrt{x + 2} &= y\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that we take the negative square root because if\n\n$$\nx \\leq 3\n$$\n\nis the domain of $f$, then the range of the inverse is\n\n$$\nf^{-1} \\leq 3\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with $f^{-1}(x){:}$\n\n$$\nf^{-1}(x) = 3 - \\sqrt{x + 2}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184164 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "86cc32d1-5444-5deb-9168-ba67cd8d0e69" :knowledge-point/title "Quadratic Functions Containing an Isolated Perfect Square"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/id #uuid "24c26333-1433-5c1e-991d-f29fb85f24d4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186181485}] :question/id #uuid "f9b3665f-1e6e-5b22-b4a7-a783bccbb796" :question/math-academy-id "q-222050" :question/problem "What is the inverse of $f(x) = 7 - (x + 1)^{2}$ for $x \\ge - 1$?$f^{-1}(x) =$\n{{field-1}}"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184166 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "02655639-b390-510d-9eda-3221375e7e5e" :knowledge-point/title "The Negative Square Root Case"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "986004a0-30f9-50e6-ac4c-76ab38fe22c2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{x - 7} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183344} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a81c9d-41f5-57ae-85aa-894633a2ce5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{-1}(x) = \\sqrt{x + 1} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183345} {:answer/id #uuid "e7e3893a-cb67-53c2-9a84-86eb78c7bc27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{-1}(x) =-\\sqrt{x + 1} - 7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183346} {:answer/id #uuid "16aa1fe8-845f-5558-a417-9e864c7558df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{-1}(x) =-\\sqrt{x - 7} - 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183347} {:answer/id #uuid "5e179551-6419-5fe2-8125-d9507f6aa237" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "f^{-1}(x) =-\\sqrt{x + 7} + 1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183348}] :answer-field/id #uuid "3748a2b3-6e6e-58cf-b9a7-b382cfce2fe2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186183343}] :question/id #uuid "e2e323d3-460f-5bcb-be71-a754f4dd2852" :question/math-academy-id "q-46347" :question/problem "Find the inverse of the function $f(x) = (x + 1)^{2} + 7$ for $x \\le - 1$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186184790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 1759218